  "normalize": false,
  "sentence_method": "one complete sentence per generation",
  "word_method": "independent word generation, not extracted from sentence audio",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "When cold weather comes, many birds move to the south.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-01.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Many animals do not remain in one place.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-02.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Moving is a normal part of their lives.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-03.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Some move to find food more easily, but others move to get away from crowded places or to survive disasters like an earthquake.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-04.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "We can compare this action to people moving for better opportunities.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-05.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Some fishes give birth in warm water and move to cold water to feed.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-06.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "text": "The most famous migration is probably that of the fish called salmon.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-07.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "text": "This fish is usually grey, but turns red when it is ready to breed.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-08.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "text": "It is born in fresh water but travels miles to salt water.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-09.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "text": "They must fight against the strong force of the river and avoid being hunted by bears, because the law of nature allows only the strongest salmon to survive.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-10.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "text": "When it is old, it returns to its birthplace in fresh water.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-11.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "text": "Then it gives birth and dies.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-12.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "text": "In the north of Europe, there is a kind of mouse.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-13.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "text": "They usually look pale, but when their homes become crowded, their colour gets brighter.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-14.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "text": "They have a crazy way of moving.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-15.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "text": "Sometimes they move all the way to the seaside, forming large groups like an army.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-16.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "text": "Many of them are killed when they fall into the sea.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-17.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "text": "Recently, scientists have studied a special kind of lobsters.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-18.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "text": "Every year, when the season of bad weather arrives, the lobsters get into a long line and start to walk across the floor of the ocean, just like soldiers marching.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-19.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "text": "Nobody knows where they go.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-20.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "text": "The reason why animals move may vary.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-21.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "text": "Maybe living things just like to travel.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-22.mp3",
      "exists": true
    }
  ],
